    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d39">

                <pb facs="0087" n="40" xml:id="pg40"/>

                <head>39. Telegram 400 to Geneva<anchor n="1" xml:id="d39-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1955-08-06">August 6, 1955, 2:41
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d39-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d39-1"/>
                <p>400. For Johnson.</p>
                <p>Do you have any clue as to source Scripps-Howard dispatch Geneva August 4 written
                    by Ludwell Denny? On surface some of information would appear to be from
                    American official source.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Dulles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
